1. Start with one letter

UNSENT is a private place to write something you might never send. Someone in West Bengal opens it on their phone, taps Write a letter, and types “I miss our late-night talks.” They select the sentence, tap Writing language → English to Banglish, and preview “Amader late-night kothagulo khub miss kori.” They can edit that version, keep their English, or save both. They seal the letter, reopen it tomorrow and make a 9:16 card with only the words they selected. Nothing in that journey sends a message to the person they wrote about.

